Kadane’s Algorithm (Maximum Subarray Sum)

What problem does it solve?

Kadane’s Algorithm is used to find the maximum sum of a contiguous
 subarray within a given array of integers (can include negative numbers).

📌 Contiguous means the elements must be next to each other.
Example

Array:
[-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4]


Maximum subarray:
[4, -1, 2, 1]


Maximum sum:
6

Core Idea (Algo Pattern)
At each index, decide:

Should we extend the current subarray, or
Start a new subarray from the current element?
If the current sum becomes negative, it’s better to reset it to the current
 element.

Key Variables

currentSum: Maximum sum ending at the current index
maxSum: Overall maximum subarray sum found so far

Algorithm Steps
Initialize:
currentSum = arr[0]
maxSum = arr[0]
Traverse the array from index 1 to n-1

For each element:

currentSum = max(arr[i], currentSum + arr[i])
maxSum = max(maxSum, currentSum
Return maxSum

Java Implementation
public class KadaneAlgorithm {

    public static int maxSubArray(int[] arr) {
        int currentSum = arr[0];
        int maxSum = arr[0];

        for (int i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
            currentSum = Math.max(arr[i], currentSum + arr[i]);
            maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, currentSum);
        }

        return maxSum;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4};
        System.out.println("Maximum Subarray Sum = " + maxSubArray(arr));
    }
}

Time & Space Complexity

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)

Why Kadane’s Algorithm is Important

Extremely efficient for large arrays
Commonly asked in FAANG / product-based company interviews
Foundation for advanced problems (2D Kadane, circular arrays)

Edge Cases

All numbers negative → returns the largest (least negative) number
Single-element array → returns that element

Real-World Use Cases

Maximum profit/loss in stock price changes
Signal processing
Data analysis and pattern recognition

